! v0.74.0 PCM test 3:  water in benzene (HF/STO-3G, IEFPCM).
!
! Low-eps solvent test:  benzene has eps = 2.27, where the conductor
! approximation behind C-PCM is least accurate.  At this eps:
!   alpha = 2pi(eps+1)/(eps-1) = 2pi * 3.27/1.27 = 16.18 (vs 2pi = 6.28
!     for the conductor limit -- big difference)
!   f_CPCM = (eps-1)/eps = 0.5595 (whereas the conductor limit is 1.0)
!
! So C-PCM and IEFPCM should give noticeably DIFFERENT G_pol here.
! This test simply checks that the IEFPCM build runs to convergence
! and that |G_pol| < |G_pol_water| (less polar -> smaller stabilization).
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%pcm     iefpcm
%eps     2.2706
%geom angstrom
O  0.000000   0.000000   0.119262
H  0.000000   0.755453  -0.477047
H  0.000000  -0.755453  -0.477047
*end
